 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 624 people. Revenue per employee of $444K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $83K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Adaptive Biotechnologies Corpor is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $4.7B market cap on $277M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -124% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $49M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -4.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 19% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 20% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $13.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 1061% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Adaptive Biotechnologies Corporation $ADPT Stock Sold by Knights of Columbus Asset Advisors LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/adaptive-biotechnologies-corporation-adpt-stock-sold-by-knights-of-columbus-asset-advisors-llc.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794479640.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Adaptive Biotechnologies (NASDAQ:ADPT) COO Julie Rubinstein Sells 11,881 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/adaptive-biotechnologies-nasdaqadpt-coo-julie-rubinstein-sells-11881-shares-of-stock-2.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794362939.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title